  "summary": "Introduced canonical staged FeeAssessment with generic non-empty ordered violations and typed policy-cause locations; validated scenario and policy identity before evaluation; accumulated every directive fee, denomination, and index failure in stable order; and constructed ScenarioFees plus existential AssessedFee values only after full success. Exact indexed slices, including equal-looking duplicates and heterogeneous fee assets, are retained through JVM-private constructors. The provisional PnL bridge now consumes assessed fees, while FeeLine, caller-selected markets, reference-equality reconciliation, and the universal FeePolicyError surface are absent. Both formatting checks, 31 fee-policy tests, and all 155 adversarial/compiler tests pass. The automated review completed scope, AC-015, staged suppression, error provenance, scenario ownership, JVM construction authority, migration, architecture, complexity, security applicability, evidence, and checkpoint axes with no findings; it changed no file, triaged no finding, and is not canonical whole-change Verify or Human Review."
